WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.501
Why won't the Germans do this?

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.402
I don't understand.

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.036
Like,
any time

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.404
you talk to an administration official,

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:06.272
they try to downplay the tensions

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.073
going on in naito,

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.508
but it's really spilling over.

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:09.275
It's really quite obvious.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:09.876
You have the Polish Prime

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.811
Minister criticizing

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:12.946
Chancellor Schultz.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:14.280
Why won't they

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.849
even just allow other countries

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:17.050
to give the leopard to?

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:17.884
No one knows for sure.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:18.785
Jake, in my mind, it's

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.220
a lack of leadership.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:20.787
The German seem

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:21.554
very reluctant

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:22.555
still to depart

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.325
from a decades old policy of ice politic,

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:26.760
where they try to make nice

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.360
with the Russians.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.695
And it's the Ukrainians

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.063
are paying the price for it.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:31.531
And one of the arguments

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:34.034
that that the Germans are making is

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:35.835
they don't want to go into this alone.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:36.703
They want the Americans

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.338
to send some Abrams tanks,

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:39.506
which the Ukrainians

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:40.673
are not really asking for,

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.076
because the fuel is different there.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.544
They're bigger. They're older.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:47.847
What's the downside of the U.S.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.549
sending a few of these tanks

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.384
just to satisfy the Germans?

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:52.752
Could that actually

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:53.586
I mean, the Russians

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:54.988
don't think of Germany as a threat,

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.523
but they certainly think of the U.S.

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:57.223
as one.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:58.591
Does that play into it?

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.059
Well, first of all,

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.660
I think
the Biden administration is right

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.861
that the weapons are better

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.196
tank than the Abrams.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:04.130
For all the logistical

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.098
and other reasons and

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:05.799
and I've been critical,

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:06.533
of course, of the Biden

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:07.700
administration in the past.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.401
But on this one,

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.170
I think if the key is to send

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.004
a dozen Abrams

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:12.439
to unlock the Germans,

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:13.039
get it done,

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.874
send over a dozen Abrams tanks,

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:15.608
and allow

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.977
then Germany and Poland and Finland

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:18.411
and others

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:20.046
who have leopards as well, two

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:21.481
to provide it to the Ukrainians.

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:22.382
Because, look,

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:24.250
time is not on our side here.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.585
We talk about a spring offensive

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.320
either by the Russians happening

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.422
sometime in March, about five weeks away

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.790
or preferably

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:31.291
the Ukrainians

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.359
launching their own offensive beforehand.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.527
And it's going to take time

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.762
to deliver the tanks,

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:36.096
the train,

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:36.963
the Ukrainians up

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.364
to set up the supply lines

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.933
for logistics and maintenance.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:40.733
Let's get it moving.

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.102
And I'm hopeful

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:43.837
I suspect this will get unlocked

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:45.004
in the next couple of days or so.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:45.905
Do you think

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.340
how do you think it's going to go along?

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.442
I think they're all moving toward

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.710
a solution whereby

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:52.912
the Poles and Germans at the

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:53.780
highest level will get it done.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.115
We had the German foreign minister today

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.950
say, well, if the Poland's want to send

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.518
if the Poles want to send it, go ahead.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:00.019
We won't mind. Oh, okay. Right.

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.287
And so now

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:02.655
now the Poles are saying, well,

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.023
we want to hear from the chancellor.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:04.591
So it looks like

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:05.825
they're inching their way toward this.

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.694
But look, again, if it takes a dozen

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.362
Abrams tanks to position

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.563
somewhere in western

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:11.731
Ukraine to unlock this,

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.432
let's get on with

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:14.000
the time is not on Ukrainian side.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.401
If you were secretary of defense

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:15.768
right now,

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.370
what would you be arguing

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.305
that the US should be doing that the U.S.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:20.607
is not currently doing?

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:21.941
Well, I'd send some tanks, right?

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:22.775
Like the Germans.

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.110
I still think they need attack

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.112
those long range precision missiles.

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:28.381
Why not to strike deep into Russia,

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:29.883
but to strike deep in Crimea

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:32.185
to knock out those shaheed drone

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:33.286
launch points

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.288
and to knock out other logistics

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:36.723
lines of communication

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:37.624
and all those things they need.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.325
And third, the Germans

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:40.160
I'm sorry, the Ukrainians

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.227
need more air defense

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:42.795
to protect the cities

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.264
and then to protect themselves

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:45.298
going forward

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:47.066
as they move in offensive

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:48.635
Would you only give the attack arms

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:49.469
with the under

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:50.003
the provision

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:50.670
that they cannot

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.272
be used to fire into Russia,

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:53.973
they can only be used to fire

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.675
at Russian forces in Crimea?

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:57.110
Would that be like that?

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.044
That would be the rule.

00:02:58.044 --> 00:02:59.612
If that's what it takes to get them

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.948
to get attack arms to to Ukraine?

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.516
Yes, there is a concern

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:04.817
that if you start striking deep

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.986
into Russia,

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.655
that you may turn the populate

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:09.889
the Russian population

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.558
alongside

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:12.625
Vladimir Putin

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:13.259
and you don't

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.627
want to unnecessarily escalate.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:15.962
So in my mind,

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:16.896
A, provide them attack

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.298
arms, allow them to reach deep

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:19.532
into eastern Ukraine

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:21.167
and deep into southern Ukraine,

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.435
to include Crimea

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:24.103
again, to knock out those launch points

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.138
and logistic centers.

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:25.972
Take a listen

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:27.373
to the new chairman of the House

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.041
Foreign Affairs

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:28.942
Committee, Michael McCaul,

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:30.310
Republican of Texas,

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.177
talking to my college

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.045
colleague, Dana Bash

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:33.813
about the importance

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.949
of educating members of Congress

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.350
as there are a lot of,

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:37.850
as you know,

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.419
Republicans in the kind of MAGA

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:40.753
isolationist warning to those

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:42.589
who don't want to be involved in this.

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:44.190
The importance of educating them

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.292
as to why aid to Ukraine is so important.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.260
Take a listen.

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:50.296
If Ukraine falls, Chairman Xi in

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:52.165
China is going to invade Taiwan.

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:55.568
If Russia, China, Iran is putting drones

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:56.469
in Crimea

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:58.838
and North Korea, that's putting artillery

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.573
into Russia.

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:03.142
Do you agree?

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:03.710
I do.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:04.544
I've said from day one

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:06.045
that Beijing is watching very,

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.046
very closely

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:08.281
about how the United States

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:09.749
and its allies will respond.

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:10.416
And thankfully,

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:11.684
we responded

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:13.553
in a unified way comprehensively.

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:15.722
Financial sanctions, economic sanctions,

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:17.156
diplomatic sanction,

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.191
sanctions, and, of course,

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:19.025
military support

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:20.026
to push back on the Russians.

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.561
So everybody is watching.

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:22.895
I think this is a

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:23.696
smart investment

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:24.764
for the United States to continue

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.299
to provide arms,

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:28.368
ammunition and assistance to Ukrainians,

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:29.969
because Ukraine in defeat would be

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:31.404
would go a long way

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:33.139
toward knocking back one of our clear

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:33.640
near peer

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.475
or previously near peer competitors.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:38.845
One of the knocks on the U.S.

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:41.114
government's support for this war

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:43.750
has to do with how

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:44.817
how good for profits

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:45.885
this is for

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.553
the military industrial complex.

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:49.622
You used to work for Raytheon,

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:51.424
which is a leading defense contractor,

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:52.225
which won

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:54.560
a massive $1.2 billion contract

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.028
with the Pentagon.

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:56.462
You don't work for them anymore. I know.

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:58.498
But how do you counter

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.333
that argument that, you know,

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.668
I'm not saying that I believe this,

00:05:01.668 --> 00:05:02.602
but you only want this

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:04.570
because the military industrial complex

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:05.238
is getting fat.

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:07.640
I want this because

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.475
we are now in a

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:10.143
in a struggle

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.978
between autocracy and democracy.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:12.412
This will be

00:05:12.412 --> 00:05:14.080
the struggle of the 21st century

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:14.714
and it's important

00:05:14.714 --> 00:05:15.915
that the Western democracies

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:17.550
band together and beat back

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.052
the Russian autocrat called

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.086
Vladimir Putin,

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:21.554
because like we said earlier,

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:23.556
a Jinping sitting in Beijing watching

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:25.291
and he's watching how we react

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:26.659
and how we will respond.

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:27.994
And every day that we continue

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.495
to remain unified and support

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:30.830
the Ukrainians is a day

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.832
that he backs off from any tensions

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:34.133
he might have against Taiwan.

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:35.401
Do you talk to any of the House

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:36.202
Republican leadership?

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:37.070
They're in charge now,

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:37.570
and I think there are

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:38.838
a lot of Republicans

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:39.906
who think the way you do

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:41.674
about international affairs,

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:43.409
who are worried about the Marjorie

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:44.677
Taylor Greene's and the other,

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:46.312
I don't want to

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:47.714
add whatever they are, isolationists,

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:48.181
whatever people

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:48.748
that were reluctant

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:49.916
to get involved in Ukraine

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:50.983
worry about their voices

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:52.652
getting louder and more powerful.

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:53.753
I've talked to senior members

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:54.620
on both sides of the aisle

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:55.788
and on the Republican side,

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:58.091
I think most most Republicans understand

00:05:58.091 --> 00:05:59.659
this is important to do to do this

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:00.960
to support the Ukrainians,

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.295
that it's in our long term

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:04.430
national security interests to do so.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.632
So I'm confident at the end of the day,

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:07.700
that will prevail.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.501
I want to ask you,

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:09.369
there's a new book

00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:10.603
from your friend and colleague,

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:12.872
Mike Pompeo called Never Give an Inch.

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:14.874
And there's an excerpt of mentions you.

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:17.143
Not that many, but this is one of the few

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:18.411
he writes on July 19th.

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:18.878
20, 20.

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:20.246
As I was on a flight back to D.C.,

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:21.047
White House Chief of Staff

00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:22.181
Mark Meadows called me.

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:24.517
Mike Esper is not going to make it,

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:25.184
he said.

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:26.452
He added that the president told him

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:28.654
that he wanted me to do all hat

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:29.055
and take

00:06:29.055 --> 00:06:30.423
on leading the Department of Defense

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:32.325
as an additional duty.

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:33.159
I told Meadows that

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:34.994
I thought that was a nutty idea.

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:36.429
Now, you survived

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:37.697
until a few months later.

00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:39.832
What did you did?

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:41.367
Had you
heard about that before that he wanted

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:43.236
Pompeo to run the State Department

00:06:43.236 --> 00:06:44.137
and the Pentagon?

00:06:44.137 --> 00:06:44.570
Yeah, no,

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:45.605
I had not heard about that,

00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:47.039
but of course, I knew,

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:47.673
you know,
when I pushed

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:49.375
back on the President's desire to use

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.177
active duty forces in the

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:52.078
protests in D.C.

00:06:52.078 --> 00:06:53.613
in early June, and then I came out

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:55.181
and publicly spoke out against it.

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:56.382
I knew I was on thin ice

00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:57.283
from that point forward.

00:06:57.283 --> 00:06:59.419
So as I write in my memoir,

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:00.153
there were a number of things

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:01.621
I had to do to advance the ball

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:02.622
to protect the nation.

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:03.489
The national security,

00:07:03.489 --> 00:07:04.290
what we we're trying to do,

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:05.258
and I continue to do

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:06.926
those as I push back on

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:08.628
what I thought were not smart ideas.

00:07:08.628 --> 00:07:10.530
And my game plan was get to the election.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:11.197
And fortunately,

00:07:11.197 --> 00:07:12.832
I was able to do so under wasn't

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:13.933
I guess, a need to do.

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:16.302
Mike Pompeo, you got to the election.

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:17.804
Thanks so much for being here.

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:18.871
Appreciate it.

00:07:19.272 --> 00:07:20.673
Mark Esper, former secretary of defense.

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:21.173
He.

